From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 03:16:57 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] soc: apple: sleep: let T8132 leave the perf state and
 DCS to firmware

The T8132 commit waits for the SoC perf state and DCS to reach their
sleep states and, if they do not in time, steps them down from the
CPU, as T8140 does. The macOS 25G83 trace has no CPU write for either
on T8132: its firmware gets there by itself.

Add t8132_cpu_perf_down (default on, behaviour unchanged). Off, the
commit only waits for both, as macOS does, so one deep run can tell
whether the CPU-side writes play a part in the failed T8132 resume.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
---
 drivers/soc/apple/sleep.c | 16 +++++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/soc/apple/sleep.c b/drivers/soc/apple/sleep.c
index b097a3d1a8..acf83a480c 100644
--- a/drivers/soc/apple/sleep.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/apple/sleep.c
@@ -3359,6 +3359,11 @@ static void t8132_arm_dram_check(struct apple_sleep *s)
 	s->check_ranges = c->nranges;
 }
 
+static bool t8132_cpu_perf_down = true;
+module_param(t8132_cpu_perf_down, bool, 0644);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(t8132_cpu_perf_down,
+		 "T8132: step the SoC perf state and DCS down from the CPU at the commit if the firmware has not (default: on)");
+
 static int t8132_sleep_commit(unsigned long unused)
 {
 	struct apple_sleep *s = apple_sleep;
@@ -3372,13 +3377,18 @@ static int t8132_sleep_commit(unsigned long unused)
 	apple_sleep_arm_wd2(s);
 	/*
 	 * macOS has the SoC at its sleep perf state and DCS at state 4 by now. Its firmware
-	 * does that, with no write from the CPU. T8140's way gets the same states here.
+	 * does that, with no write from the CPU. T8140's way gets the same states here,
+	 * unless t8132_cpu_perf_down is off: then only wait for them, as macOS does.
 	 */
-	if (sleep_perf_wait(s->clk_perf + CLK_PERF_SOC, SOC_SLEEP_STATE)) {
+	if (sleep_perf_wait(s->clk_perf + CLK_PERF_SOC, SOC_SLEEP_STATE) &&
+	    READ_ONCE(t8132_cpu_perf_down)) {
 		writel(SOC_SLEEP_STATE, s->clk_perf + CLK_PERF_SOC);
 		sleep_perf_wait(s->clk_perf + CLK_PERF_SOC, SOC_SLEEP_STATE);
 	}
-	apple_sleep_dcs_down(s);
+	if (READ_ONCE(t8132_cpu_perf_down))
+		apple_sleep_dcs_down(s);
+	else
+		sleep_dcs_wait(s, DCS_SLEEP_STATE);
 	t8132_sleep_mcc_stop(s);
 
 	/* Gates twice, the fourth voter, gates. On macOS the voter reads 0 already. */
-- 
